---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="StackPilot Ecosystem — gODtECH" description="How StackPilot, gODtECH Steward, and gODtECH FORGE fit together.">
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-dot"></span> gODtECH ecosystem</div>
      <h1><span class="gradient-text">Build it. Keep it healthy.</span><br />Govern the work around it.</h1>
      <p class="hero-copy">StackPilot, gODtECH Steward, and gODtECH FORGE are independent tools with intentionally separate responsibilities. The ecosystem is stronger because each product stays focused.</p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="button button-primary" href="https://github.com/gODtECH-Ctl-Create/StackPilot" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">StackPilot ↗</a>
        <a class="button" href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/@godtech/steward" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Install Steward ↗</a>
        <a class="button" href="https://github.com/gODtECH-Ctl-Create/gODtECH-FORGE" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Explore FORGE ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="section-kicker">Three clear jobs</div>
        <h2>Use the smallest tool that solves the problem.</h2>
        <p class="section-lead">No product needs another product to perform its core job. Connections happen through stable public interfaces.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid grid-3">
        <div class="card"><span class="card-label">01 · ORCHESTRATE</span><h3>gODtECH FORGE</h3><p>Prepares context, classifies risk, plans work, manages approvals, persists runs, and collects evidence around AI-assisted engineering.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><span class="card-label">02 · BUILD</span><h3>StackPilot</h3><p>Chooses supported project paths, renders golden-path repositories, and owns stack-aware validation and readiness.</p></div>
        <div class="card"><span class="card-label">03 · MAINTAIN</span><h3>gODtECH Steward</h3><p>Scans existing repositories deterministically, exposes health findings, and applies only explicit safe remediation.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="section-head">
        <div class="section-kicker">The boundary</div>
        <h2>They can work together without becoming one system.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="flow">
        <div class="flow-step"><b>01</b><strong>FORGE prepares</strong><span>Repository facts, task context, risk, workflow and evidence boundaries.</span></div>
        <div class="flow-step"><b>02</b><strong>StackPilot builds</strong><span>When the workflow needs a supported project foundation or golden path.</span></div>
        <div class="flow-step"><b>03</b><strong>Steward checks</strong><span>When the repository needs deterministic health or safe maintenance.</span></div>
        <div class="flow-step"><b>04</b><strong>FORGE verifies</strong><span>External deterministic results can become workflow evidence without duplicating their domain logic.</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="callout">
        <div><h2>Different tools. One clean engineering story.</h2><p>StackPilot creates the foundation. Steward keeps the repository healthy. FORGE governs the work around both.</p></div>
        <a class="button button-primary" href="https://github.com/gODtECH-Ctl-Create/gODtECH-Steward" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">View Steward →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
